{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139175-hedge-beast-familiar-alternate-familar-2","id":1139175,"title":"Hedge Beast Familiar (Alternate Familar 2)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-10T07:07:23-07:00","id":1139175,"title":"Hedge Beast Familiar (Alternate Familar 2)","content":"I was just rereading CtL a while ago, and was reminded about Hedge Beasts. I wondered if it is reasonable for a mage with Fate magic to form a familiar bond with a Hedge Beast.<br /> <br /> Fate seems to be the Arcanum of choice regarding all things Fay, and the animals would work well IMO as familiars. I know this is a little trickier than the normal spirit/ghost/goetia line of familiars since it starts to venture into crossover territory (though regular interaction between changeling type and mage type characters is not the reason for getting the familiar, and it will not necessarily become a thing). Also, as I understand it, Hedge Beasts don't suffer any sort of essence bleed, but they may still want to enter into the relationship for protection or adventure.<br /> <br /> The Familiar Bond spells always seemed a bit special to me, in that they can create a bond between the mage and a spirit etc. that grants qualities that seem would normally require Space. That leads me to think that the ability to create a Familiar Bond might be universal in some way or other to all Arcana, much like the ability to summon a Supernal creature. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","user":"Newes","date":". 09-10-2017, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T13:52:09-07:00","id":1140000,"title":"","content":"I like crossover, and I like this idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T18:04:42-07:00","id":1140052,"title":"","content":"The Familiar spell and the bond it creates need not be a requirement for a mage to call something her familiar. Especially with Hedge Beasts, who are already well accustomed to the idea of forming contracts and bargains with another being. Which can be created via Fate spells, so in the end its still &quot;use Fate magic to get a familiar,&quot; I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T18:33:31-07:00","id":1140057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139175-hedge-beast-familiar-alternate-familar-2?p=1140052#post1140052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Familiar spell and the bond it creates need not be a requirement for a mage to call something her familiar. Especially with Hedge Beasts, who are already well accustomed to the idea of forming contracts and bargains with another being. Which can be created via Fate spells, so in the end its still &amp;quot;use Fate magic to get a familiar,&amp;quot; I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, what you lose out on are Connectec Sympathy, shared senses, and the ability to use a Reach to cast on remote targets your familiar can perceive. You can probably gain benefits better than that though by simply picking your &quot;familiar&quot; wisely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T01:46:21-07:00","id":1140112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139175-hedge-beast-familiar-alternate-familar-2?p=1140057#post1140057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, what you lose out on are Connectec Sympathy, shared senses, and the ability to use a Reach to cast on remote targets your familiar can perceive. You can probably gain benefits better than that though by simply picking your &amp;quot;familiar&amp;quot; wisely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but there doesn't really seem to be a reason why Spirit mind or death should be able to Grant you those particular abilities. That's why I wonder if the familiar Bond shouldn't be a spell available to every subtle Arcana with some variation like attack spells. I almost feel it would work better as some sort of attainment like supernal summoning. <br /> <br /> Though of course it is correct that there is no in- character reason that your familiar has to involve a familiar Bond spell. You can have a cool sanctum without actually taking the sanctum merit and you can have a cool magical animal companion and call it you're familiar without the familiar Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T11:35:23-07:00","id":1140254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139175-hedge-beast-familiar-alternate-familar-2?p=1140112#post1140112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but there doesn't really seem to be a reason why Spirit mind or death should be able to Grant you those particular abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those Arcana correspond to both parts of the human soul-anatomy and common invisible entities subject to Essence bleed. The Familiar bond only lasts as long as neither party (nor the creator of the bond, if that's a separate person) chooses to end it and while it lasts the two beings are metaphysically flush with each other and able to swap their magical resources regardless of distance. The creation of a potent sympathetic link doesn't require Space any more than compelling a spirit to possess someone requires Mind \u2014 the powerful connection is forged as a peripheral effect of your being a mage meshing a bit of your soul with something that has some relation to the stuff of human souls and their byproducts.<br /> <br /> There's a case to be made for this meaning Fate 4 could be used for an all-purpose version of the Familiar spell that can meddle with any of the three varieties of ephemeral being, but the reason Familiars work as they do is because they're types of being that can do things like &quot;die&quot; in one place and resurrect themselves in another. A Hedge-Beast Companion doesn't have the same needs and capabilities as spirits and the like, and Fate already gives you the ability to do some of the things that having a mobile magical observer at your disposal enables.<br /> <br /> There's also the matter of how if you're bringing in a Hedge Beast but don't plan to actually bring in the Hedge, then there's not much difference between that and having a normal familiar bound to an animal through a third party. What's the actual purpose, here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T03:25:46-07:00","id":1140472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139175-hedge-beast-familiar-alternate-familar-2?p=1140254#post1140254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those Arcana correspond to both parts of the human soul-anatomy and common invisible entities subject to Essence bleed. The Familiar bond only lasts as long as neither party (nor the creator of the bond, if that's a separate person) chooses to end it and while it lasts the two beings are metaphysically flush with each other and able to swap their magical resources regardless of distance. The creation of a potent sympathetic link doesn't require Space any more than compelling a spirit to possess someone requires Mind \u2014 the powerful connection is forged as a peripheral effect of your being a mage meshing a bit of your soul with something that has some relation to the stuff of human souls and their byproducts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. That was a pretty good justification as to why the familiar bond works the way it does with the ephemeral entities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139175-hedge-beast-familiar-alternate-familar-2?p=1140254#post1140254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a case to be made for this meaning Fate 4 could be used for an all-purpose version of the Familiar spell that can meddle with any of the three varieties of ephemeral being, but the reason Familiars work as they do is because they're types of being that can do things like &quot;die&quot; in one place and resurrect themselves in another. A Hedge-Beast Companion doesn't have the same needs and capabilities as spirits and the like, and Fate already gives you the ability to do some of the things that having a mobile magical observer at your disposal enables.<br /> <br /> There's also the matter of how if you're bringing in a Hedge Beast but don't plan to actually bring in the Hedge, then there's not much difference between that and having a normal familiar bound to an animal through a third party. What's the actual purpose, here?</div> </div> </div> </div>It started because I like, and wanted to port in, the idea of familiars as friends and physical entities (as they are portrayed in Ars Magica and many stories), rather than the more alien options in Mage (even if the mage options bear more similarity to original familiar inspirations from myth and folklore). Hedge Beasts seemed perfect.<br /> What are the Fate abilities you refer to that give you some of the same things a mobile observer does?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T03:55:30-07:00","id":1140478,"title":"","content":"Oaths Fulfilled, probably some creative variation on Shared Fate, Sworn Oaths, mucking with Destiny at the higher end. These allow you to crudely monitor the goings on of the target and share some level of metaphysical &quot;meshing&quot; as well as ensuring that they're working (and probably want to work) in your best interests and are empowered when doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}